meta {
  name: 09 Grant Branch A Operator Permissions
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/manage/{{baOperatorUserId}}/branch-permissions
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAdminToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "branchId": "{{baBranchId}}",
    "items": [
      { "moduleKey": "accession", "permissionKey": "accession:internal_referral_order__pick_up_the_sample", "allowed": true },
      { "moduleKey": "accession", "permissionKey": "accession:internal_referral_order__receive_the_sample", "allowed": true },
      { "moduleKey": "accession", "permissionKey": "accession:internal_referral_order__accept_the_sample", "allowed": true }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  **Setup - grant the Branch A operator the internal-referral receiving permissions:**
  Pick Up, Receive and Accept. The receiving side of an internal transfer is
  RBAC-enforced by these keys; on Accept, RULE 1 clones the sample into Branch A's
  In-House list and **rehomes the report's branch to Branch A** - which is what makes
  Branch A the "processing branch" for the LIS gate. As in step 08, the grant needs
  the `accession` module both enabled on Branch A (step 05) and assigned to this user
  (step 07).
}
